{"id":"u-9bf52e3f-0e33-484e-beb1-76f30fb5df99","src":"community","title":"FBEOD ni lor","author":"lorvxnz","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/qg0kwH-fbeod-l","desc":"My goal with this FBEOD program is to build muscle, improve strength, and develop a balanced physique while giving extra attention to my abs, chest, back, and arms. I keep volume low but make every working set count through good form, enough weight, and training close to failure.\n\nI train **3 times per week**. Week 1 is **Monday: A, Wednesday: B, Friday: A**, while Week 2 is **Monday: B, Wednesday: A, Friday: B**. My rest days are Tuesday, Thursday, Saturday, and Sunday. I can still walk or do light activities on rest days, but I avoid hard lifting so I can recover properly.\n\nI use low volume to get enough stimulus without unnecessary fatigue. Most exercises have only 1–2 hard sets. I train most exercises at **1–2 RIR (RPE 8–9)**, meaning I could still perform 1–2 good reps. Isolation exercises can reach **0–1 RIR (RPE 9–10)**. Failure means I cannot complete another clean rep with proper form.\n\nI rest **3–5 minutes between hard compound sets** such as presses, rows, squats, and RDLs. For isolation exercises such as curls, triceps, lateral raises, calves, and abs, I rest around **2–3 minutes**. I do not rush rest because I want enough recovery to perform my next set properly.\n\nI use proper form by controlling the weight, using a full comfortable range of motion, and avoiding momentum. If my technique breaks down badly, I consider the set finished.\n\nI use **double progression** to improve over time. If an exercise is 2 × 5–8, I work toward 8 reps on both sets while maintaining my target RIR. Once I reach the top of the range, I increase the weight slightly and build the reps back up.\n\nFor nutrition, I focus on whole foods and enough protein for muscle growth and recovery. A general target is **1.6–2.2 g/kg of protein daily**. Good affordable sources include eggs, chicken, fish, pork, beef, milk, Greek yogurt, tofu, and other protein-rich foods. I also eat enough carbohydrates for training energy and healthy fats.\n\nRecovery is part of training. I aim for **7–9 hours of sleep**, stay hydrated, and avoid unnecessary extra training when I am not recovered. If my performance consistently decreases, I reduce fatigue instead of immediately adding more volume.\n\nMy main rule is: **train hard, use good form, rest enough, eat well, recover, and progressively improve.** I do not need a huge number of exercises or sets; I need consistent, high-quality training that I can progress with over time.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced","Beginner"],"goals":["Muscle","Athletics"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":80,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-12T06:27:35.486Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["FULL BODY A","FULL BODY B","FULL BODY A"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Pec Deck (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}],"note":"use a 15-30 incline"},{"n":"T-Bar Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10}]},{"n":"Squat (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9}]},{"n":"Seated Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10}]},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10}]},{"n":"Calf Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10}]},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Neutral Grip)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi"